ments":2,"created_at":"2021-01-02T19:14:35Z","updated_at":"2023-10-25T00:18:36Z","closed_at":"2021-03-01T16:51:33Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Version\r\n3.0.5\r\n\r\n### Reproduction link\r\n[https://codepen.io/hisrootness/pen/GRjxNzL](https://codepen.io/hisrootness/pen/GRjxNzL)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n1. Use `createApp` to encapsulate a `<g>` element with children representing SVG shapes.\r\n2. Mount the app inside an existing `<svg>` element.\r\n\r\n### What is expected?\r\nThe nodes added by Vue app to the parent SVG image should be instances of `SVGElement` and should be able to affect the drawing.\r\n\r\n### What is actually happening?\r\nThe app nodes are added to DOM, but they are not instances of `SVGElement` and they don't draw anything on the parent SVG image.\r\n\r\n---\r\nIn Vue2 I was able to add my component to existing SVG image (not created by Vue). In Vue3 SVG rendering only seems to work when the `<svg>` element itself is rendered by the Vue instance.\r\n\r\nHere is example when the drawing works (the only difference from repro is that `id=\"app\"` is above the `<svg>` element instead _on_ it):  \r\nhttps://codepen.io/hisrootness/pen/MWjVbLJ\r\n\r\nAnd here is an example showing that it used to work in Vue 2:\r\nhttps://jsfiddle.net/hisrootness/7nkob98v/1/\r\n\r\n<!-- generated by vue-issues. DO NOT REMOVE -->","closed_by":{"login":"yyx990803","id":499550,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5OTU1MA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/499550?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yyx990803","html_url":"https://github.com/yyx990803","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yyx990803/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yyx990803/followi